Specifically, the text-input fallback chain (ACTION_SET_TEXT → retry →
clipboard + ACTION_PASTE) in Actions.setText and the "click self, else a
clickable ancestor, else a gesture at the node centre" approach in
Actions.click are adapted from PokeClaw's tool/impl/InputTextTool.java and
service/ClawAccessibilityService.java.

What was NOT taken from those projects: their automatic tapping of system
"Allow" / permission dialogs, their type-all-input-masks behaviour,
QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES, and their debug HTTP server. Forsion Hands does none of
these; it neither auto-confirms system prompts nor exposes any network surface.
